# GenApp Environment Configuration
# =================================

# —  —  —  — PRIVATE (set as Railway env vars, never in client code) —  —  —  —
# Generate a random secret for session cookie signing:
#   python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# Required for stable sessions across app restarts.
# If not set, sessions reset on every restart (random per-start key).

# DATABASE_URL — PostgreSQL connection string (Railway provides this automatically).
# Local dev: postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/genapp
# Do NOT use SQLite (DB_PATH) — Railway free tier has no persistent disk.

# COOKIE_SECURE — set to "true" when serving over HTTPS (Railway always).
# Set to "false" for local HTTP development.

# —  —  —  — PUBLIC (visible in browser, no secrets) —  —  —  —
# These values are referenced in app.js and are safe to be seen by clients:
#   - Role names: "admin", "client", "agent" (used for UI logic only)
#   - API endpoints: /api/login, /api/me, /api/logout, /api/users,
#     /api/orders, /api/transactions, /api/admin/delete-data,
#     /api/orders/stream, /api/transactions/stream, /api/health
#   - Price labels: clientPricePerGen, agentPricePerGen,
#     supplierPricePerGen, dieselPricePerLiter
#
# Permission enforcement is ALWAYS server-side (requireAuth/requireAdmin
# middleware in auth-server.js). UI role checks are convenience only.
